License scope
=============

This repository contains components with different file-level notices. It does
not assign one blanket license to every source, dataset, or historical file.

1. Geth library files and certificate library additions

   The Geth library files under geth/core/, geth/eth/, and geth/internal/ retain
   their original go-ethereum copyright and GNU Lesser General Public License
   version 3 or later notices. Certificate library and native test files with
   SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later retain that declaration.

   Full terms: licenses/COPYING.LESSER, together with licenses/COPYING.

2. New standalone command

   geth/cmd/gas-certificate/*.go declares GPL-3.0-or-later in each file header.
   This includes its JSON adapter and adapter tests.

   Full terms: licenses/COPYING.

3. Additional benchmark and historical material

   Preserve the copyright, attribution, and license declarations carried by
   each file. An LGPL declaration in a native benchmark fixture applies to
   that fixture. A patch retains the license scope of the files it changes.

   Some preserved historical command, Python, JavaScript, Solidity, input,
   generated artifact, and data files have no explicit license declaration in
   their headers. This repository does not infer or grant new terms for those
   files. The GPL/LGPL texts supplied here do not relicense third-party or
   otherwise unspecified material.

See NOTICE for source provenance and the exact origin of the license texts.
